    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d518">

                <pb facs="0530" n="524" sameAs="frus:frus1942v02/pg524"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851.01/848</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Delegation of the French National Committee in the
                        United States to the Department of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-06-11">June 11, 1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Referring to its note of May 18, the Delegation of the French National Committee
                    in the United States has the honor to send herewith to the Department of State,
                    by order of the National Committee, the text of a Memorandum<anchor n="53"
                        xml:id="d518-f1"/> which defines and elaborates the views already expressed
                    in the above-mentioned note on the conditions of Combatant France in the
                    question concerning the war status of the French possessions in America.</p>
                <p>Copy of this communication has been sent to Ambassador Drexel Biddle<anchor
                        n="55" xml:id="d518-f2"/> in London.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d518-f1" n="53" xml:id="d518-f1-content">
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Infra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d518-f2" n="55" xml:id="d518-f2-content">
                <p>Ambassador to the Polish Government in Exile at London and Minister to the
                    Governments in Exile at London of Czechoslovakia, Greece, the Netherlands,
                    Norway, and Yugoslavia.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
